                <pb facs="0526" n="422" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg422"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/819.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Puerto
                            Plata to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Puerto Plata</hi></placeName>, <lb/>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1913-04-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 1, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Arias yesterday agreed with Vasquez here to resist election of Velásquez. Cibao
                    apparently united to make war in case of election of Velasquez.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hathaway</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
